title: Lockdown
text: Eight sealed rooms. Every doorway in the block has been bricked up on the far side, so nobody can walk out. Light is not so polite about where it walks.
trick: the walls only meet corner to corner across each bricked-up doorway, so a diagonal beam slips through: red crosses three rooms by the doorways, bouncing off a mirror standing in the first one; blue must not run on down the diagonal into red's target, so a mirror in its doorway turns it into the room next door
motif: rooms (a block of eight rooms in brick bond, no doors, only gaps at the wall junctions, each with a wall straight behind it)
expect: depth>=3
---
